# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the op-fusion SHIP gates (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of
# tp4/fusion-1 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. Templates only: no tag is pushed from the
# branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the pass rule. ONE IMAGE: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-s6nt-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the approved commit
# (sed -i 's/tp4-s6nt-1/<tag>/' *.env). The cards are under development: nothing here stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# GX1 (STOP): EXACTNESS of the ship profile c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s6-nt against its control GX0 on the same image: the same prompts,
# unaudited. READ: python3 scripts/ci/parked_compare.py --control <GX0 smoke log> --parked <GX1 smoke log> --control-container <GX0 container log> --parked-container <GX1
# container log> --profile c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s6-nt: every levern_equal, levern_equal_busy and parked_equal content hash EQUAL (the
# last w2-er GX: 37 of 37), compared above 0, the parked judge with 0 problems under the lever band. Any difference is NO-GO for shipping. TELEMETRY (C2_TELEMETRY=1,
# scripts/ci/card_telemetry.py): the read-only ARC sidecar samples every chip once a second through the smoke step (AICLK and the limiter holding it, power, current,
# temperature, kernel NOPs); read telemetry-smoke/telemetry-summary.txt beside the result; the first [TELEMETRY] line must say decode check ok. It runs on the host and
# reads only. CHECKPOINT (C2_MODEL_REPO and C2_MODEL_REVISION, qwen_c2_checkpoint.py): the job serves ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b at b4c84d42903a, the checkpoint
# production serves beside this profile, from its own converted-weight directory and with its catalog entry's request numbers laid over the profile's
# (serving_c2_contract.checkpoint_limits: the default answer and the output ceiling), as a production boot runs; the keys are the same in G1, GX0, GX1 and G2, so GX0 and
# GX1 differ by the profile alone. READ: the container log holds "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b@b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4 key=..." once,
# a "weight cache ...: found" line and the worker's "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint bound ..." line (the smoke step passes c2_smoke_check.py --expect-checkpoint; the prefix gate
# checks every arm's log). NO-TIER READ (tp4/s6-notier): no "host tier on" line and no "host tier restore slice on" line; the checkpoint store at 16 GiB; the "[PINDIAG]
# text-only boot: vision tower skipped" line once per engine process and no vision weight load in the boot log; the "[PINDIAG] host heap trimmed after warmup" line once (or
# its skipped line, never a traceback); every other ship-6 read unchanged (the governor's install line, WC's engaged line and its one octo decline). Duration (estimate): 15
# minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-s6nt-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s6-nt
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,parked_equal,parked_budgets,levern_equal,levern_equal_busy
C2_MODEL_REPO=ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b
C2_MODEL_REVISION=b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4
C2_SMOKE_PARTIAL=exactness ship arm: its test list is fixed by the protocol, so concurrent8_steady is not run
C2_BOX_MINUTES=40
C2_TELEMETRY=1
